IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`

-- Income Tax Act 1947 — PARTS 7 TO 9: FROM INCOME TO ASSESSABLE INCOME.
--
-- Part 7 (special ascertainment): non-resident shipping (ss 27, 28), the
-- anti-avoidance surcharge (s 33A), the transfer-pricing surcharge and
-- documentation (ss 34E, 34F). The other Part 7 regimes (insurers, Lloyd's,
-- financial-instrument accounting, amalgamations, redomiciled companies,
-- tonnage tax) produce an adjusted income figure that is an input.
-- Part 8 (statutory income, ss 35-36C). Part 9 (assessable income, ss 37-37S):
-- losses, donations, group relief, carry-back, the EIS cash payout.
--
-- Source: ../source/ITA1947.txt lines 16643-24855.

§ `Parts 7 to 9 — statutory and assessable income`

§§ `Statutory income (s 35)`

-- s 35(1): "the statutory income is the full amount of the person's income for
-- the year preceding the year of assessment from each source of income after
-- the deduction provided under subsection (2)". (2), (2A): capital allowances
-- (ss 16-20) are deducted "firstly, against income from any trade, business,
-- profession or vocation; and secondly, against income from any other source".
-- Unused allowances carry forward under s 23.
DECLARE `Statutory income` HAS
    `from trades and professions`  IS A NUMBER
    `from other sources`           IS A NUMBER
    `total`                        IS A NUMBER
    `allowances unused`            IS A NUMBER

@ref s 35(1)-(2A)
GIVEN `trade income`     IS A NUMBER
      `other income`     IS A NUMBER
      allowances         IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Statutory income`
`the statutory income, trade income` `trade income` `, other income` `other income` `, allowances` allowances MEANS
    `Statutory income` WITH
        `from trades and professions` IS `trade after`
        `from other sources`          IS `other after`
        `total`                       IS `trade after` PLUS `other after`
        `allowances unused`           IS `left after other`
    WHERE
        `trade` MEANS IF `trade income` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `trade income`
        `against trade` MEANS IF allowances GREATER THAN `trade` THEN `trade` ELSE allowances
        `trade after` MEANS `trade` MINUS `against trade`
        `left` MEANS allowances MINUS `against trade`
        `against other` MEANS IF `left` GREATER THAN `other income` THEN `other income` ELSE `left`
        `other after` MEANS `other income` MINUS `against other`
        `left after other` MEANS `left` MINUS `against other`

§§ `Losses and donations (s 37)`

-- s 37(3)(a): trade losses are deducted, "(i) firstly, any balance of such loss
-- which remains unabsorbed at the end of the basis period for the previous year
-- of assessment; (ii) secondly, the amount incurred during the basis period".
-- (3)(c), (3A): donations of money to the Government or an IPC: "2.5 times the
-- amount" for donations from 1 January 2016 to 31 December 2026 (and 2009-2014),
-- "3 times" for 2015, otherwise twice. (7): donations are deducted after
-- losses. (8): unused donations carry forward, but any balance not used by the
-- fifth YA after the YA of the donation "is disregarded". (12), (14): a
-- company's losses and donations are disregarded unless "not less than 50%" of
-- its shares are held by the same persons on both dates (or exempted, (16)).
@ref s 37(3)(c), (3A)
GIVEN amount     IS A NUMBER
      `date given`  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction for a donation of` amount `made on` `date given` MEANS
    amount TIMES `the multiple`
    WHERE
        `between` a b MEANS `date given` AT LEAST a AND `date given` AT MOST b
        `the multiple` MEANS
            BRANCH IF `between` (YMD 2015 1 1) (YMD 2015 12 31)  THEN 3
                   IF `between` (YMD 2009 1 1) (YMD 2014 12 31) OR `between` (YMD 2016 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) THEN 2.5
                   OTHERWISE 2

DECLARE `Assessable income` HAS
    `losses used`               IS A NUMBER
    `losses carried forward`    IS A NUMBER
    `donations used`            IS A NUMBER
    `donations carried forward` IS A NUMBER
    `assessable income`         IS A NUMBER

@ref s 37(1), (3)(a), (7), (8), (12)
GIVEN `statutory income`        IS A NUMBER
      `losses brought forward`  IS A NUMBER
      `loss of the basis period` IS A NUMBER
      `donation deductions available` IS A NUMBER
      `same shareholders test met, or not a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Assessable income`
`the assessable income from statutory income` `statutory income` `, losses brought forward` `losses brought forward` `, current loss` `loss of the basis period` `, donations` `donation deductions available` `, shareholders:` `same shareholders test met, or not a company` MEANS
    `Assessable income` WITH
        `losses used`               IS `losses used`
        `losses carried forward`    IS `losses` MINUS `losses used`
        `donations used`            IS `donations used`
        `donations carried forward` IS `donations` MINUS `donations used`
        `assessable income`         IS `after losses` MINUS `donations used`
    WHERE
        `losses` MEANS IF `same shareholders test met, or not a company` THEN `losses brought forward` PLUS `loss of the basis period` ELSE `loss of the basis period`
        `donations` MEANS IF `same shareholders test met, or not a company` THEN `donation deductions available` ELSE 0
        `losses used` MEANS IF `losses` GREATER THAN `statutory income` THEN `statutory income` ELSE `losses`
        `after losses` MEANS `statutory income` MINUS `losses used`
        `donations used` MEANS IF `donations` GREATER THAN `after losses` THEN `after losses` ELSE `donations`

@ref s 37(8)
GIVEN `YA of the donation's basis period` IS A NUMBER
      ya                                  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an unused donation from YA` `YA of the donation's basis period` `may still be deducted in YA` ya IF
    ya AT MOST `YA of the donation's basis period` PLUS 5

@ref s 37(12), (14)
GIVEN `percent held by the same persons on both dates` IS A NUMBER
      `exempted under s 37(16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a company's losses and donations survive, same shareholders holding` `percent held by the same persons on both dates` `, exempted:` `exempted under s 37(16)` IF
        `percent held by the same persons on both dates` AT LEAST 50%
    OR  `exempted under s 37(16)`

§§ `Group relief (s 37B) and carry-back (s 37D)`

-- s 37B(2), (3): a transferor may transfer a qualifying deduction to a claimant
-- of the same group, if on the last day of the basis period they are members of
-- the same group, have accounting periods ending on the same day, and have
-- elected; "2 Singapore companies are members of the same group if — (a) at
-- least 75% of the total number of issued ordinary shares in one company are
-- beneficially held ... by the other; or (b) at least 75% ... in each ... by a
-- third Singapore company"; (4) with at least 75% of residual profits and
-- assets; (5) indirect holdings multiply.
@ref s 37B(2)-(5)
GIVEN `percent held, directly or through the chain` IS A NUMBER
      `entitled to 75% of residual profits and assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `same accounting year end`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `both elected`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `group relief may be transferred, holding` `percent held, directly or through the chain` `, residual entitlement:` `entitled to 75% of residual profits and assets` `, same year end:` `same accounting year end` `, elected:` `both elected` IF
        `percent held, directly or through the chain` AT LEAST 75%
    AND `entitled to 75% of residual profits and assets`
    AND `same accounting year end`
    AND `both elected`

-- s 37B(5): the fractions in a chain are multiplied.
@ref s 37B(5)
GIVEN fractions IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the effective holding through the chain` fractions MEANS
    CONSIDER fractions
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 1
    WHEN f FOLLOWED BY rest THEN f TIMES `the effective holding through the chain` rest

-- s 37D(1), (3), (5): a qualifying deduction may be carried back against the
-- assessable income of the immediately preceding YA, the lower of the deduction
-- available and that income, and "must not exceed $100,000". (1A): for YA 2020
-- or 2021, back 3 YAs, earliest first.
@ref s 37D(1), (3), (5)
GIVEN `qualifying deduction`              IS A NUMBER
      `assessable income of the preceding YA` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the carry-back allowed, deduction` `qualifying deduction` `, preceding income` `assessable income of the preceding YA` MEANS
    `lowest` (`lowest` `qualifying deduction` `assessable income of the preceding YA`) 100000
    WHERE
        `lowest` a b MEANS IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `The Enterprise Innovation Scheme cash payout (s 37R)`

-- s 37R(1), (4): for YAs 2024-2028, in lieu of the listed enhanced deductions or
-- allowances, an eligible person may elect (for selected expenditure of at least
-- $400) a cash payout of "A × 20%", A the lower of the selected expenditure and
-- $100,000.
@ref s 37R(1), (4)
GIVEN ya                     IS A NUMBER
      `selected expenditure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the EIS cash payout for YA` ya `on selected expenditure of` `selected expenditure` MEANS
    BRANCH IF ya LESS THAN 2024 OR ya GREATER THAN 2028 THEN 0
           IF `selected expenditure` LESS THAN 400       THEN 0
           OTHERWISE (IF `selected expenditure` LESS THAN 100000 THEN `selected expenditure` ELSE 100000) TIMES 20%

§§ `Part 7 — special ascertainment`

-- s 27(2): with a certificate from its home tax authority, a non-resident
-- shipowner's profits accruing in Singapore are "a sum bearing the same ratio to
-- the sums receivable in respect of the carriage of passengers, mail, livestock
-- and goods shipped in Singapore as the total profits for that period bear to the
-- total sum receivable". s 28: the same for air transport and cable.
@ref s 27(2), s 28
GIVEN `receipts from carriage shipped in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
      `total profits`  IS A NUMBER
      `total receipts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Singapore profits of a non-resident shipowner, Singapore receipts` `receipts from carriage shipped in Singapore` `, total profits` `total profits` `, total receipts` `total receipts` MEANS
    IF `total receipts` EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE `receipts from carriage shipped in Singapore` TIMES `total profits` DIVIDED BY `total receipts`

-- s 27(4): without a certificate complying with (3), "the profits accruing in
-- Singapore are deemed to be a sum equal to 5% of the full sum receivable on account
-- of the carriage of passengers, mail, livestock and goods shipped in Singapore".
-- (6): no tax where the Comptroller decides the call is casual and further calls
-- improbable. (Added after the independent test pass listed it as not expressible.)
@ref s 27(2), (4), (6)
GIVEN `a certificate complying with s 27(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a casual call`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `receipts from carriage shipped in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
      `total profits`  IS A NUMBER
      `total receipts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Singapore profits of a non-resident shipowner, certificate:` `a certificate complying with s 27(3)` `, casual call:` `a casual call` `, Singapore receipts` `receipts from carriage shipped in Singapore` `, total profits` `total profits` `, total receipts` `total receipts` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a casual call` THEN 0                                                                  -- (6)
           IF `a certificate complying with s 27(3)`
              THEN `the Singapore profits of a non-resident shipowner, Singapore receipts` `receipts from carriage shipped in Singapore` `, total profits` `total profits` `, total receipts` `total receipts`   -- (2)
           OTHERWISE `receipts from carriage shipped in Singapore` TIMES 5%                           -- (4)

-- s 33A(2): for YA 2023 on, where tax is imposed under the anti-avoidance rule
-- (s 33), "a surcharge equal to 50% of the amount of tax or the additional amount
-- of tax". (4): payable within one month after notice, despite an objection.
-- s 34E(1): for YA 2019 on, a transfer-pricing adjustment under s 34D(1A) carries
-- "a surcharge equal to 5% of the amount of the increase or reduction".
@ref s 33A(2)
GIVEN ya    IS A NUMBER
      tax   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 33A surcharge for YA` ya `on additional tax of` tax MEANS
    IF ya AT LEAST 2023 THEN tax TIMES 50% ELSE 0

@ref s 34E(1)
GIVEN ya          IS A NUMBER
      adjustment  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the transfer-pricing surcharge for YA` ya `on an adjustment of` adjustment MEANS
    IF ya AT LEAST 2019 THEN adjustment TIMES 5% ELSE 0

-- s 34F(1)-(3): for YA 2019 on, a company, firm or trust must prepare
-- transfer-pricing documentation for each related-party transaction "(a) if the
-- gross revenue ... for the basis period concerned is more than $10 million;
-- or (b) if documentation ... is required to be prepared for a transaction ...
-- in the basis period immediately before", unless exempt by rules. (7): to be
-- furnished within 30 days of a notice. (8): failure is an offence, fine up to
-- $10,000.
@ref s 34F(1)-(3), (7), (8)
GIVEN ya                    IS A NUMBER
      `gross revenue`        IS A NUMBER
      `required the previous basis period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exempt by rules`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `transfer-pricing documentation is required for YA` ya `, gross revenue` `gross revenue` `, required before:` `required the previous basis period` `, exempt:` `exempt by rules` IF
        ya AT LEAST 2019
    AND NOT `exempt by rules`
    AND (`gross revenue` GREATER THAN 10000000 OR `required the previous basis period`)
